Source: octagonos-facetui
Section: kde
Priority: optional
Maintainer: The octagonOS Project <noreply@octagonos.dev>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               cmake,
               extra-cmake-modules,
               kwin-dev,
               qt6-base-dev,
               libkf6coreaddons-dev,
               libkf6config-dev,
               libkf6svg-dev | kf6-ksvg-dev,
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: facetui-kwin-effect
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: FacetUI glass effect for KWin
 The specular edge and the rim darkening that turn a blurred, translucent
 surface into glass, as a KWin effect. Transcribed from the AGSL that ships on
 the Android edition of octagonOS, and checked against the same NumPy both are
 lit by.
 .
 KWin's effect API is not binary compatible across versions, so this must be
 built against the KWin it runs on. The dependency below is generated from the
 library it linked against, which enforces that.

Package: facetui-plasma-style
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: FacetUI Plasma style and colour scheme
 Translucent surfaces with a one-pixel hairline, and the colour scheme the rest
 of the desktop is drawn in. Two of the three things a surface needs to be
 glass; KWin's blur effect is the third, and facetui-kwin-effect lights it.
 .
 The tint is not in these files: Plasma replaces the theme's stylesheet with
 the live colour scheme, so the surfaces take the system's colour rather than
 one baked in.

Package: facetui-icon-theme
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: breeze-icon-theme, hicolor-icon-theme
Description: glass octagons for application and freedesktop icons
 A glass octagon with a glyph on it, at eight sizes, for the standard
 freedesktop icon names and for the application ids of programs a desktop tends
 to have. Everything else inherits from Breeze.
 .
 The glass is rendered from the same code the Android icon pack draws its
 adaptive-icon backgrounds with.

Package: facetui-plymouth-theme
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, plymouth, initramfs-tools | dracut
Description: FacetUI boot splash for Plymouth
 The octagonOS mark, rendered from FacetUI's own shader maths, with a
 passphrase prompt for encrypted disks that does not depend on a font being
 present in the initramfs.
 .
 Installing this makes it the default boot theme and rebuilds the initramfs,
 because Plymouth runs from the initramfs and a theme that is only in
 /usr/share changes nothing about the next boot.

Package: octagonos-facetui
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         facetui-kwin-effect,
         facetui-plasma-style,
         facetui-icon-theme,
         facetui-plymouth-theme,
Description: FacetUI, selected by default
 Ships the system defaults that make FacetUI the desktop's theme rather than
 one of its options, and a Global Theme entry so it can be re-selected after a
 user changes something.
 .
 Naming a look-and-feel package is not enough on its own: its defaults are only
 applied when someone selects it, and every component reads kdeglobals and
 plasmarc directly. So those are shipped as system configuration, which a
 user's own choices still override.
